.TH XEONDESKTOP\-SESSION 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xeondesktop\-session \- start a XeonDesktop session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xeondesktop\-session
.RI [ xd\-compositor\ options ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xeondesktop\-session
starts a XeonDesktop session.
Display managers run it from
.IR /usr/share/wayland\-sessions/xeondesktop.desktop ,
which lists XeonDesktop among the sessions to log on to.
.PP
It sets up the session's environment, then runs
.BR xd\-compositor (1)
with its own arguments:
.IP \(bu 2
.BR XDG_SESSION_TYPE=wayland ,
.B XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=XeonDesktop
and
.BR XDG_SESSION_DESKTOP=xeondesktop ;
.IP \(bu
variables that make Firefox, Qt, SDL and Java programs use Wayland
.RB ( MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND ,
.BR QT_QPA_PLATFORM ,
.BR SDL_VIDEODRIVER ,
.BR _JAVA_AWT_WM_NONREPARENTING );
.IP \(bu
the variables in
.I ~/.config/environment.d
(System Properties > Advanced > Environment Variables writes them there),
as systemd's environment generator merges them;
.IP \(bu
if formats customized in Regional and Language Options need a locale that
is no longer installed, the formats without the customizations.
.PP
When the compositor exits, however it exits, it stops
.I xeondesktop\-session.target
in the user manager (and with it
.I graphical\-session.target
and the session's services) and takes the session's variables back out of
the user manager's environment.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/environment.d/*.conf
The user's environment variables.
.TP
.I /usr/share/wayland\-sessions/xeondesktop.desktop
The session entry for display managers.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-compositor (1),
.BR environment.d (5),
.BR systemd.special (7)
